slug: conversation-runtime
what: a spec for the runtime a human-facing conversation needs - a
  suspension that waits for a person, an intake driver over frames and
  slots, and the boundary that leaves a caller owning only the data of
  its own domain. Written from a working implementation that is being
  offered upstream.
touches: specs/conversation.md (new), BACKLOG.md  (NO source, NO tests)
note: neighbours intent-classify.md (recognition) and llm-agentic.md
  (Durable). Does not edit either.
